{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/vapour-density-rmm/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/vapour-density-rmm.html","area":"students","kind":"topic","title":"Vapour Density & Relative Molecular Mass | Chemistry Foundations","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"mb-4 flex items-center justify-between\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition flex items-center\">\n        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Foundations\n      </a>\n      <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n        <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">\n          <span id=\"topic-progress-text\" data-bidemy=\"progress-text\">0% Complete</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"w-24 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full overflow-hidden\" data-bidemy=\"progress\">\n          <div id=\"topic-progress-bar\" class=\"h-full bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-400 to-orange-500 transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </nav>\n\n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -weight-hanging text-amber-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Vapour Density &amp; Relative Molecular Mass\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Understanding the relationship between vapour density and molecular mass, and how to calculate them.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-amber-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• Define vapour density and relative molecular mass</li>\n          <li>• State the relationship between VD and RMM</li>\n          <li>• Calculate RMM from vapour density</li>\n          <li>• Determine molecular formula from empirical formula and VD</li>\n          <li>• Solve problems involving vapour density</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: Definitions -->\n      <section id=\"section-1\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          Definitions\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-100 to-orange-100 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-amber-500\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-2\">Vapour Density (VD)</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2\">The vapour density of a gas is the ratio of the mass of a certain volume of the gas to the mass of an equal volume of hydrogen gas under the same conditions of temperature and pressure.</p>\n              <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded font-mono text-center text-sm mt-2\">\n                VD = Mass of V volume of gas / Mass of V volume of H₂\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-100 to-indigo-100 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\">Relative Molecular Mass (Mᵣ)</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2\">The relative molecular mass is the mass of one molecule of a substance compared to 1/12th the mass of a carbon-12 atom. It has no units.</p>\n              <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded font-mono text-center text-sm mt-2\">\n                Mᵣ = Sum of relative atomic masses in formula\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -info-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"info\">info</span>Important Note</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Vapour density is only defined for gases or substances that can be vaporized. It is a ratio and has no units.</p>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: The Key Relationship -->\n      <section id=\"section-2\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          The Key Relationship\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-green-100 to-teal-100 p-6 rounded-lg text-center mb-4 border-2 border-green-300\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg text-gray-800 mb-2\">The Relationship</p>\n            <p class=\"text-4xl font-bold text-green-700 mb-2\">Mᵣ = 2 × VD</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">or equivalently: VD = Mᵣ / 2</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3\">Why is this relationship true?</h4>\n            <ol class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li class=\"flex gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-5 h-5 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0\">1</span>\n                <span>By Avogadro's Law, equal volumes of gases contain equal numbers of molecules</span>\n              </li>\n              <li class=\"flex gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-5 h-5 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0\">2</span>\n                <span>VD = Mass of n molecules of gas / Mass of n molecules of H₂</span>\n              </li>\n              <li class=\"flex gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-5 h-5 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0\">3</span>\n                <span>VD = Mass of 1 molecule / Mass of 1 H₂ molecule</span>\n              </li>\n              <li class=\"flex gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-5 h-5 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0\">4</span>\n                <span>VD = Mᵣ / 2 (since H₂ has Mᵣ = 2)</span>\n              </li>\n            </ol>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Remember</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Hydrogen (H₂) has a relative molecular mass of 2. This is why we multiply VD by 2 to get Mᵣ.</p>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: Worked Examples -->\n      <section id=\"section-3\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Worked Examples\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-amber-50 text-left font-semibold text-amber-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-amber-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-amber-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Example 1: Calculate Mᵣ from VD</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-5\">\n                <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">A gas has vapour density of 16. Calculate its relative molecular mass.</p>\n\n                <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-amber-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Formula:</strong> Mᵣ = 2 × VD</p>\n                  </div>\n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Substitute:</strong> Mᵣ = 2 × 16</p>\n                  </div>\n                  <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                    <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\">Answer: Mᵣ = 32 (This is O₂)</p>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-blue-50 text-left font-semibold text-blue-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-blue-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-blue-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Example 2: Calculate VD from Mᵣ</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-5\">\n                <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Calculate the vapour density of carbon dioxide (CO₂).</p>\n\n                <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Find Mᵣ:</strong> Mᵣ(CO₂) = 12 + (2×16) = 44</p>\n                  </div>\n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-indigo-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Formula:</strong> VD = Mᵣ / 2</p>\n                  </div>\n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Substitute:</strong> VD = 44 / 2 = 22</p>\n                  </div>\n                  <div class=\"bg-blue-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                    <p class=\"text-blue-800 font-semibold\">Answer: VD = 22</p>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-green-50 text-left font-semibold text-green-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-green-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-green-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Example 3: Find Molecular Formula</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-5\">\n                <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">A compound has empirical formula CH₂O and vapour density 30. Find its molecular formula.</p>\n\n                <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Find Mᵣ</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-green-700 mt-1\">Mᵣ = 2 × VD = 2 × 30 = 60</p>\n                  </div>\n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Find empirical formula mass</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-blue-700 mt-1\">CH₂O = 12 + (2×1) + 16 = 30</p>\n                  </div>\n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Find n</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-purple-700 mt-1\">n = Mᵣ / empirical mass = 60 / 30 = 2</p>\n                  </div>\n                  <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                    <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\">Molecular formula = (CH₂O)₂ = C₂H₄O₂</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-green-700 text-sm\">This is ethanoic acid (acetic acid)</p>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Common VD Values -->\n      <section id=\"section-4\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          VD Values of Common Gases\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n          <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse border border-gray-300 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <thead class=\"bg-amber-600 text-white\">\n              <tr>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-left\">Gas</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">Formula</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">Mᵣ</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">VD</th>\n              </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody class=\"bg-white\">\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2\">Hydrogen</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-mono\">H₂</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">2</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-bold text-amber-700\">1</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2\">Oxygen</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-mono\">O₂</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">32</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-bold text-amber-700\">16</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2\">Nitrogen</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-mono\">N₂</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">28</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-bold text-amber-700\">14</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2\">Carbon dioxide</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-mono\">CO₂</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">44</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-bold text-amber-700\">22</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2\">Ammonia</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-mono\">NH₃</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">17</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-bold text-amber-700\">8.5</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2\">Chlorine</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-mono\">Cl₂</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">71</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-bold text-amber-700\">35.5</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2\">Methane</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-mono\">CH₄</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">16</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center font-bold text-amber-700\">8</td>\n              </tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Practice Problems -->\n      <section id=\"section-5\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-amber-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. A gas has vapour density of 8. Calculate its relative molecular mass and identify the gas.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Mᵣ = 2 × VD = 2 × 8 = <strong>16</strong></p>\n                <p>A gas with Mᵣ = 16 is <strong>methane (CH₄)</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. Calculate the vapour density of SO₂.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Mᵣ(SO₂) = 32 + (2×16) = 64</p>\n                <p>VD = Mᵣ / 2 = 64 / 2 = <strong>32</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. A hydrocarbon has empirical formula CH and vapour density 39. Find its molecular formula.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Mᵣ = 2 × 39 = 78</p>\n                <p>Empirical mass = 12 + 1 = 13</p>\n                <p>n = 78 / 13 = 6</p>\n                <p>Molecular formula = <strong>C₆H₆</strong> (benzene)</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. State the relationship between vapour density and relative molecular mass.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p><strong>Mᵣ = 2 × VD</strong> or <strong>VD = Mᵣ / 2</strong></p>\n                <p class=\"mt-1\">The relative molecular mass is twice the vapour density.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">5. Why is VD compared to hydrogen and not oxygen?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Hydrogen is the lightest gas (Mᵣ = 2), making calculations simple. The factor of 2 in the relationship Mᵣ = 2 × VD comes from the molecular mass of H₂ being 2.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n      <section id=\"section-6\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-50 to-orange-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-amber-200\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways for WAEC/JAMB/NECO</h3>\n          <ul class=\"text-amber-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n            <li>• <strong>VD = Mᵣ / 2</strong> and <strong>Mᵣ = 2 × VD</strong></li>\n            <li>• Vapour density is defined relative to hydrogen</li>\n            <li>• Hydrogen has Mᵣ = 2, so VD = 1</li>\n            <li>• Use VD to find Mᵣ, then determine molecular formula</li>\n            <li>• VD = (mass of gas) / (mass of equal volume of H₂)</li>\n            <li>• Remember: VD is a ratio, has no units</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Complete Topic Button -->\n      <div class=\"mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200\">\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Ready to Complete?</h3>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">View all sections, then take the quiz to mark this topic as complete.</p>\n          </div>\n          <button id=\"topic-complete-btn\" disabled=\"\" class=\"px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gray-300 text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed opacity-50 flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-medium\">\n            <span class=\"mi -lock mr-2\" data-mi=\"lock\">lock</span>\n            <span>Complete (0% viewed)</span>\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n  \n\n\n<div data-bidemy=\"quiz\"></div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-amber-50 to-orange-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n    .content-card {\n      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);\n      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n    }\n    .accordion-content {\n      max-height: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      transition: max-height 0.3s ease-out;\n    }\n    .accordion-content.open {\n      max-height: 2000px;\n    }\n    .step-card { transition: all 0.2s ease; }\n    .step-card:hover { transform: translateX(4px); }\n    #topic-complete-btn { transition: all 0.3s ease; }\n    #topic-complete-btn:not(:disabled):hover { transform: scale(1.02); }"],"quiz":{"topicId":"vapour-density-rmm","subject":"chemistry","passingScore":60,"questions":[{"question":"The relationship between vapour density (VD) and relative molecular mass (Mᵣ) is:","options":["Mᵣ = VD","Mᵣ = 2 × VD","Mᵣ = VD / 2","Mᵣ = VD²"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Mᵣ = 2 × VD. The molecular mass is twice the vapour density."},{"question":"What is the vapour density of oxygen (O₂)?","options":["8","16","32","14"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Mᵣ(O₂) = 32. VD = Mᵣ/2 = 32/2 = 16"},{"question":"A gas has VD = 22. What is its Mᵣ?","options":["11","22","44","88"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Mᵣ = 2 × VD = 2 × 22 = 44 (This is CO₂)"},{"question":"Vapour density is defined with reference to:","options":["Oxygen","Nitrogen","Hydrogen","Air"],"correct":2,"explanation":"VD is the ratio of mass of gas to mass of equal volume of hydrogen."},{"question":"The vapour density of hydrogen gas is:","options":["1","2","0.5","4"],"correct":0,"explanation":"H₂ has Mᵣ = 2. VD = Mᵣ/2 = 2/2 = 1"},{"question":"A compound has empirical formula CH₂ and VD = 14. Its molecular formula is:","options":["CH₂","C₂H₄","C₃H₆","C₄H₈"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Mᵣ = 2 × 14 = 28. Empirical mass = 14. n = 28/14 = 2. Formula = C₂H₄"},{"question":"Which gas has VD = 8?","options":["O₂","N₂","CH₄","CO₂"],"correct":2,"explanation":"VD = 8 means Mᵣ = 16. CH₄ has Mᵣ = 12 + 4(1) = 16"},{"question":"Vapour density has:","options":["Units of g/cm³","Units of g/mol","No units","Units of kg/m³"],"correct":2,"explanation":"VD is a ratio of two masses, so it has no units."}]},"tracker":{"topicId":"vapour-density-rmm","topicTitle":"Vapour Density & Relative Molecular Mass","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}